hakulex
Copyright (c) 2026 Ken

hakulex is a rich text editor for Vue 3, built on Lexical. It follows haklex
(https://github.com/Innei/haklex), a React rich text editor built on Lexical:
its document format, its behavior and its visual design are haklex's.

The editor, the renderer, the plugins' interfaces and the Vue bindings were
written anew for Vue. Parts that do not depend on a framework were adapted
from haklex's source code, in particular:

  - packages/litexml and packages/litexml-cli: reading and writing LiteXML
  - packages/headless: turning a document into Markdown
  - packages/diff-core and packages/diff: comparing two documents
  - packages/plugin-image-editor: cropping, mosaic and annotation helpers

together with tests for them, and smaller pieces elsewhere.

